00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:01.940
The fleet starts on January 10th, 2027, and races approximately 3,000 nautical miles

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.520
from Marina, Lanza Rote in the Canary Islands to Antigua in the Caribbean.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.460
The Royal Ocean Racing Club organizes the race.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:13.220
It is a major fixture on the offshore calendar and attracts international teams chasing a fast

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:13.980
Atlantic crossing.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.860
The challenge is a familiar one for Shawier and Roberts, but there is plenty to work out.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:23.300
They will be studying sail choices, looking at how Amira 4 performs in different wind

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.520
conditions and trying to find the fastest route across.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:28.280
Weather and roting are a big part of that puzzle.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:33.660
Shire recently produced a six-part YouTube series analyzing the 2026 Root Durum.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.400
