00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.880
The priority is to finish safely and learn more about the boat.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:57.860
Conditions permitting, they also want to improve on their 2023 crossing time of nine days,

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.420
12 hours and 26 minutes.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:04.620
The boat is close to 50% faster at some points of sale, so if they get good weather conditions

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.380
they would like to beat their previous time.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.220
Time for plain sailing, an IMO CA60 is designed to be self-writing after a capsize.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:16.200
The keel carries several tons of ballast at the bottom of a long, weighted fin.

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.240
When the boat is inverted, that ballast sits above the center of buoyancy and creates

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.880
a strong writing moment that rolls the hull upright again.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.620
The rule exists because a solo skipper cannot leave the boat to perform an external recovery,

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.180
and must be able to continue racing after a knockdown or full inversion.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:35.940
In practice, the system has allowed several vendry globe and root-do-rum skippers to resume

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:40.680
